RUN: %PLC -c --fpic %S/oop_shapes_lib.st -o %t.lib.o
RUN: %COMPILE -i %S/oop_shapes_lib.st %S/oop_shapes_main.st %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s
RUN: %COMPILE --generate-external-constructors -i %S/oop_shapes_lib.st %S/oop_shapes_main.st %t.lib.o && %RUN | %CHECK %s
RUN: mkdir -p %t.d
RUN: %PLC --constructors-only -c --fpic %S/interface_constructors_includer.st -i %S/oop_shapes_lib.st -o %t.d/a.o
RUN: %PLC -c --single-module --fpic %S/interface_constructors_includer.st -i %S/oop_shapes_lib.st -o %t.d/b.o
RUN: %PLC -c --fpic %S/interface_constructors_includer.st -i %S/oop_shapes_lib.st -o %t.d/c.o
RUN: cc -shared %t.d/a.o %t.d/b.o -o %t.d/libab.so
RUN: cc -shared %t.d/a.o %t.d/c.o -o %t.d/libac.so

oop_shapes_lib.st is compiled to its own object. It declares an abstract
function block that implements an interface, an abstract class, final and
overriding methods, STRING[n] and ARRAY properties, a program with a method and
an action, a function block with an action, inline types in members, method
locals, VAR_TEMP, function locals and globals, nested inline types in a TYPE,
an array of function blocks, and a generic function. The program includes it,
links that object, and extends the abstract function block. Then other objects
that include oop_shapes_lib.st are linked into one shared library without the
object built from oop_shapes_lib.st. Only that object may define the symbols
generated for these declarations.

